engine biome(1.0)
language js(typescript)

// `RootEntity` and concrete aggregate classes (`User`, `Role`) expose public
// setters for hydration properties (`id`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `version`,
// `username`, `department`, `name`). They exist so MikroORM's `accessor: true`
// mapping can hydrate private backing fields without `@ts-expect-error` or
// boilerplate persistence records/mappers.
//
// Under D-03, this rule enforces strict domain encapsulation at build time:
// application and presentation code must go through factories and domain
// methods. Direct property assignment is forbidden.
//
// Scoped in biome.json to the layers that must not mutate aggregates directly:
// cqrs, controllers, services, mappers, jobs, application. The persistence and
// domain trees are excluded: the ORM hydrates through these setters, and the
// aggregate itself owns its internal lifecycle via `onUpdate()`.

`$aggregate.$property = $value` as $assignment where {
  not $aggregate <: `this`,
  $property <: r"^(?:id|createdAt|updatedAt|version|username|department|name)$",
  register_diagnostic(span=$assignment, message="Do not assign aggregate properties directly via setters. These setters exist only for MikroORM hydration; application code creates aggregates through factories (e.g. User.create) and mutates them through domain methods (e.g. user.rename), which maintain aggregate invariants, versioning, and event tracking.", severity="error")
}
